;; gen.device: the device lowerings (experimental), a module of gen.clj
;; outside its core (DESIGN.md §9, the device decisions). A staged program
;; (gen.array.stage) as generated JVM code (gen.device.jvm) or as one Metal
;; kernel through MLX (gen.device.metal): what kernel/run's and importance
;; sampling's :device option and gen.inference.device/run-chains run when
;; it is on the classpath. Without it a :device run falls back to the
;; handler and says so (:device-fallback). gen.clj is its one dependency:
;; the JVM lowering compiles with the JDK's own compiler (javax.tools: a
;; JDK, not a JRE); Metal needs the MLX backend (its native libraries and
;; binding, README) and the JVM option --enable-native-access=ALL-UNNAMED.
;;
;; A dependent takes it as a git dependency on gen.clj's repository with
;; :deps/root "ext/device", at the commit of the gen.clj it uses:
;;
;;   gen.clj/device {:git/url "…gen.clj" :git/sha "…" :deps/root "ext/device"}
;;
;; It brings gen.clj from the same checkout. In gen.clj's own repository
;; the :device alias puts it on the classpath (with :test for its tests).
{:paths ["src"]
 :deps {gen.clj/gen.clj {:local/root "../.."}}}
